  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "The graph of the cubic $y=P(x)$ passes through the points $(1,0)$, $(-1,0)$, $(0,1)$ and $(2,1)$. Determine $P(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(x)=\\frac{1}{3}(2x-3)(x-1)(x+1)$.",
      "worked": "By the Factor Theorem, the roots $1$ and $-1$ give\n$$P(x)=(x-1)(x+1)(ax+b).$$\nUsing $P(0)=1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(0)&=(-1)(1)b\\\\1&=-b\\\\b&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $P(2)=1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(2)&=(2-1)(2+1)(2a-1)\\\\1&=3(2a-1)\\\\1&=6a-3\\\\a&=\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(x+1)\\left(\\frac{2}{3}x-1\\right)\\\\P(x)&=\\frac{1}{3}(2x-3)(x-1)(x+1).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
